cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its outputs, please cite the paper."
title: "Continuous Risk Pricing of Tokenized Private Credit Using Zero-Knowledge Attested Factor Reporting"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for a calibrated Monte Carlo simulation of
  zero-knowledge attested predicate reporting in tokenized private credit
  markets. The simulation evaluates a zero-knowledge attested reporting regime
  (monthly cadence) against a conventional opaque reporting regime (quarterly
  cadence) across four credit-state scenarios, with parameters calibrated to
  real benchmark data from the Cliffwater Direct Lending Index and the VanEck
  BDC Income ETF. Headline finding: 33.1% reduction in maximum monthly price
  drop under correlated stress, with peak conditional value at risk preserved.
